From: Project Luma <luma@local>
Subject: [PATCH] Enable ScreenShield for the explicit greetd mobile session

GNOME Shell normally treats a sufficiently new GDM service as the capability
probe for ScreenShield. The isolated FP6 bake-off deliberately keeps greetd
as its rollback-capable session launcher, while GNOME Mobile's power manager
requires a non-null ScreenShield.

Allow the launcher to opt this one session into ScreenShield without changing
the behavior of ordinary desktop or non-Luma sessions.
---
 js/ui/main.js | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/js/ui/main.js b/js/ui/main.js
index 554316e..2312ad1 100644
--- a/js/ui/main.js
+++ b/js/ui/main.js
@@ -247,7 +247,11 @@ async function _initializeUI() {
     magnifier = new Magnifier.Magnifier();
     locatePointer = new LocatePointer.LocatePointer();
 
-    if (LoginManager.canLock())
+    // GNOME Shell normally uses GDM presence as the lock-screen capability
+    // probe. The isolated FP6 bake-off is intentionally launched by greetd,
+    // but its mobile power manager still requires ScreenShield. Enable the
+    // shield only for the explicitly marked greetd candidate session.
+    if (LoginManager.canLock() || GLib.getenv('LUMA_GREETD_SESSION') === '1')
         screenShield = new ScreenShield.ScreenShield();
 
     inputMethod = new InputMethod.InputMethod();
